Z||000000||Seanh||05-16-2001||11:39 PM||||Well, I go out for lunch and get in my car, and craked it over till it started getting annoying (1600w battery, so I got tired before IT did) Anyway, I pulled the coil wire and checked for spark, nothing. So I thought it might be the coil, it was just replaced about 3 weeks ago, and iv had some trouble with it before. I had my old one in the car, so I tried it and still nothing. I pulled the module and swithed it with my old one and bam! Started right up. So my 3 week Module took a crap. I bought it from Advance Auto parts, so I'm taking it back in the morning since it has 1 yr replacment. It is however the GP Sorensen brand, because thats all they carry. I tried to get the accel or AC delco brand, but they don't have it stock any time and would be a special order, so I just took what they had. Why would this just die like that? I always run my engine bay cooling fan. I installed it correctly (heat shield on top and grease on bottem) so what could go wrong? Is this brand just crap? Thanks<P>PS: Taijiguy, I'll save you the trouble and say that this problem is most likly due to the neon's on my car somwhow screwing up the module, even while there off!<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
