Z||000005||Seanh||05-17-2001||10:05 PM||||I didn't remove the neons, however they were completly shut off and not connected to the car power, so they really had no way to hurt the car, unless the car itself is just mad.<P>My distributor story is a long one. The old distributor was very odd, non-fiero or anything near it. I couldn't get parts for it, so I just got a used distributor (oddly enough from Taijiguy) and installed it. It had the module on it from the old car, but I changed mine on my old distributor before breaking it, so I had the new one anyway, so I just installed it. The old module was working ok, but I figured it wouldn't hurt to change it to troubleshoot my bad gas milage problem.<P>I did give thought that one of the connectors was not holding, and it worked because I changed the module back to the old one, but today I changed it back to check on that and it still didn't work with all the connects making contact. So, Im pretty sure its the module. Damn generic brand crap. Its all AC Delco from now on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Topknot||05-17-2001||10:16 PM||||Yea ya need to keep a pocket full of those pesky modules, been there...!<P>but as for the bad gas mileage,<BR>1 - Did you check or replace the O2 sensor yet?  Seems to be a major cause of crappy mixing in the engine.<BR>2 - How about sparks, wires, air filter, and or air sensors.  All wonderful things to consider.<P>Topknot=]<BR>||||reg||1
